# Prompting BI blog rules

Astro 5 static blog deployed to GitHub Pages at https://promptingbi.com. Content lives in `src/content/blog/` as markdown. Every push to `main` auto-deploys via GitHub Actions; a daily scheduled build also publishes future-dated posts when their date arrives.

## Folder stages

```
src/content/blog/
  backlog/              # ideas / outlines — NOT loaded by Astro (never on site)
  drafts/               # WIP — in collection, keep draft: true (filtered out of site)
  published/            # live (or future-dated scheduled) — draft: false
    YYYY-MM/            # month buckets from the post date, e.g. 2026-08/
```

Promote by moving the file: backlog → drafts → `published/YYYY-MM/`. Filename stays `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`. Agents: focus on `drafts/` unless asked about backlog or published. Images stay in `public/images/YYYY/MM/` — do not nest or move them with the post.

## Creating a new post

Preferred: run `npm run new-post "My Post Title"` (scaffolds into `drafts/` + image folder). Or create `src/content/blog/drafts/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` with EXACTLY this front matter shape:

```markdown
---
title: "Post Title Here"
date: 2026-07-20T09:00:00Z
permalink: "2026/07/20/post-slug-here"
description: "One-sentence teaser. Shown on homepage, RSS, and meta description."
featured: /images/2026/07/some-image.png   # optional
draft: true                                 # keep true in drafts/; false when moving to published/YYYY-MM/
# Editor-only: EMP episode that inspired the post (not rendered on site)
source:
  episode: 544
  title: "Using Harnesses for Fabric Projects"
  notion: "https://app.notion.com/p/36de74c69c1880fdbbfbef7c346cd3b1"
  transcript: "transcripts/ep-544.txt"
---
```

Rules:
- `permalink` must be `YYYY/MM/DD/slug` matching the date — preserves the WordPress-era URL structure
- `date` must be ISO with Z suffix; future dates publish automatically on the daily build
- To publish: move file to `published/YYYY-MM/` (YYYY-MM from the post date) and set `draft: false`. URLs do not change (`permalink` is the route). Do not move images.
- slug = kebab-case; `description` under 160 characters
- `source` is optional editor/agent metadata (episode, Notion URL, local transcript path). Never render it on the site.
- Transcripts live in `transcripts/ep-{N}.txt`. Fetching one always writes there. Creating or editing a post always reads from there first (Notion/YouTube only on a miss). Never dump transcripts in `backlog/` or the repo root.

## Prompts library (`/prompts/`)

Full copy-paste artifacts — instruction pages, agent briefs, DAX validation queries, notebook patterns. A post shows a slice; the artifact page holds the complete version. That duplication is intentional.

Preferred: `npm run new-prompt "Artifact Title" <category-id>`. Or create `src/content/prompts/<slug>.md`:

```markdown
---
title: "Artifact Title"
description: "One-sentence summary shown on the /prompts/ index."
category: agent-briefs        # an id from src/lib/prompt-categories.mjs
date: 2026-08-19T09:00:00Z
updated: 2026-09-01T09:00:00Z  # optional
format: markdown               # badge text: markdown, dax, python
source:
  permalink: "2026/08/05/inside-an-mcp-execution-session"  # must match a real post
draft: true                    # false to publish
---
```

Rules:
- Flat folder, no staging. URL is `/prompts/<filename>/`, so the filename is the permanent slug.
- `category` ids in `src/lib/prompt-categories.mjs` are permanent — they're the anchors on `/prompts/`. Array order controls section order.
- `source.permalink` must match an existing post's permalink; a mismatch warns at build and renders unlinked.
- Both directions of the post ↔ artifact link are generated. Never write them by hand.
- Never link from a published artifact to a `draft: true` one (dead link).
- Page shape: a sentence or two of setup, the artifact in a fenced block, then a short "Adapting it" list of the load-bearing lines. No "Takeaways" section; that's for posts.

## Images

- Store in `public/images/YYYY/MM/` (mirror the post date)
- Reference as `/images/YYYY/MM/name.png` (absolute path, no `public/` prefix)
- Always include descriptive alt text

## Voice and style

- Author: Tommy Puglia, BI consultant (Power BI / Microsoft Fabric / AI). First person, conversational, practical, opinionated but friendly
- Posts teach through worked examples with screenshots, then end with a short "Takeaways" bullet list
- Audience: Power BI / Fabric professionals learning to use generative AI well

## Do not

- Do not edit `public/CNAME`, the `site` URL in `astro.config.mjs`, or `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` unless explicitly asked
- Do not change permalinks of existing posts (breaks inbound links)
- Do not add npm dependencies without asking
